  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency assistance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following significant flooding in Pakistan in 2022, Pheto, a 15-month-old boy from Sindh Province, faced severe acute malnutrition owing to his family&apos;s poor economic conditions. His parents, both farmers, struggled to feed their family of five following losses to their crops and income. With Australia&#x2019;s support (AU$1.5 million), CARE International and local partner the Shifa Foundation provided life-saving nutrition services for children and improved food availability. It provided Pheto&apos;s family with crucial knowledge on nutrition, hygiene practices, and access to ready-to-use therapeutic food. Pheto&apos;s health showed significant improvement within three months. His mid-upper arm circumference, a key indicator of malnutrition, increased from a critical 9.5 to a healthy 11.7 centimetres. Alongside, the project helped his mother gain the knowledge and skills to ensure a balanced diet for him.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food security</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">To help address the food security crisis following floods in Pakistan in 2022, CARE distributed 1,171 kitchen gardening kits to households in Matiari District in Sindh Province, helping them to access nutritious food that could be easily harvested, prepared and consumed. The kits were complemented by training sessions, led by smart agriculture experts, to help people successfully use the kits to grow vegetables at home. Ms Kamli, who received a kitchen gardening kit and attended the training, shared that, with technical support provided by local partner Shifa Foundation, she had cultivated the first harvest of vegetables from her garden. This initiative not only encouraged sustainable living but also enhanced food security and promoted healthy lifestyles.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
